Say whether a back gesture came from an edge swipe or a key.

What: `BackGestureEvent` gets a `source: BackGestureSource` field, `EdgeSwipe` or `Key`, with no default: every
literal names its source, so `BackGestureEvent` no longer derives `Default`. The `pointer_source` table in window.rs
(patch 0003) reads it: an edge swipe stays `Touch`, synthesized; a key-driven gesture is `None`, like a key. iOS's
edge swipe sets `EdgeSwipe`. Updates the back-gesture literals in core tests, iOS, and 0006's test.

Why: a back gesture can come from a key or button with no pointer behind it (Android's Back key and navigation-bar
button, which parallax-android sends as a `BackGestureEvent`), so `Window::pointer_source()` must not report a touch
for it. A default would silently pick one of the two behaviours for any literal that forgot the field.

Depends on: 0003 (`pointer_source` table and its test), 0006 (its test's gesture literal).

Test: two rows in `pointer_source_names_the_device_and_synthesis_of_each_event` (window.rs): edge swipe back (touch,
synthesized) and back key (none).

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

